   increasingly complex interactions between wildlife populations, the
   environment and human activities. In this position statement, we address
   the most important issues characterising current ungulate conservation
   and management in Europe. We present some key points arising from
   ecological research that may be critical for a reassessment of ungulate
   management in the future.},
