Abstract = {Interactions between glycans and glycan binding proteins are essential
   for numerous processes in all kingdoms of life. Glycan microarrays are
   an excellent tool to examine protein-glycan interactions. Here, we
   present a microbe-focused glycan microarray platform based on
   oligosaccharides obtained by chemical synthesis. Glycans were generated
   by combining different carbohydrate synthesis approaches including
   automated glycan assembly, solution-phase synthesis, and chemoenzymatic
   methods. The current library of more than 300 glycans is as diverse as
   the mammalian glycan array from the Consortium for Functional Glycomics
   and, due to its microbial focus, highly complementary. This glycan
   platform is essential for the characterization of various classes of
   glycan binding proteins. Applications of this glycan array platform are
   highlighted by the characterization of innate immune receptors and
   bacterial virulence factors as well as the analysis of human humoral
   immunity to pathogenic glycans.},
